Return a prefixed call to an unoffered tool as a tool call (TF_TOOL_UNOFFERED_PREFIX, e.g. `mcp__`).

TensorFold keeps a tool-call envelope that names a tool absent from the request's `tools` as
plain reply text. pi exposes MCP tools only inside its `codemode` tool, but after `codemode`
lists `ALL_TOOLS` (72 names) the model often writes `<function=mcp__server__tool>` as a
top-level call: the turn then ends with no call and raw markup as content (10/12 replays of
the failing session context). With `TF_TOOL_UNOFFERED_PREFIX=mcp__` (comma-separated prefixes)
the call is returned with the name as written, in the final parser (`tool_parse.callName`)
and the streamer (`tool_stream` `.call`), so the client answers "tool not found" and the model
retries through `codemode`. Other unoffered names, and an unset variable, keep stock behavior
(envelope kept as content). Test: tool_stream_test.zig "TF_TOOL_UNOFFERED_PREFIX ..." covers
final parse, off/on/other names, and the stream at every prefix boundary.

diff --git a/zig/src/server/tool_parse.zig b/zig/src/server/tool_parse.zig
index 101d6cf..82ccd6a 100644
--- a/zig/src/server/tool_parse.zig
+++ b/zig/src/server/tool_parse.zig
@@ -247,7 +247,20 @@ fn argumentsClose(a: Allocator, body: []const u8) Allocator.Error![]const u8 {
 /// The offered tool's spelling, or null when the request did not declare that name.
 fn callName(a: Allocator, c: Call, known: *const std.StringArrayHashMapUnmanaged([]const u8)) Allocator.Error!?[]const u8 {
     const name = strip(c.name);
-    return if (known.get(try std.ascii.allocLowerString(a, name))) |offered| offered else null;
+    if (known.get(try std.ascii.allocLowerString(a, name))) |offered| return offered;
+    return if (unofferedPass(name)) name else null;
+}
+
+/// TF_TOOL_UNOFFERED_PREFIX (comma-separated, e.g. ``mcp__``): a call naming an unoffered tool with one of these prefixes is
+/// returned as a call, so the client answers "tool not found" and the model can retry, instead of the envelope staying as text.
+pub fn unofferedPass(name: []const u8) bool {
+    const raw = std.c.getenv("TF_TOOL_UNOFFERED_PREFIX") orelse return false;
+    var it = std.mem.tokenizeScalar(u8, std.mem.span(raw), ',');
+    while (it.next()) |prefix| {
+        const p = std.mem.trim(u8, prefix, " ");
+        if (p.len > 0 and name.len > p.len and std.mem.startsWith(u8, name, p)) return true;
+    }
+    return false;
 }
 
 /// A named ``_openai_tool_call`` with compact JSON arguments, or null when arguments are non-finite.
